>! tav 1.0
>! target text
>#  Plain.tav — the reply when the model is unavailable, or phrased the decision into a promise.
>#
>#  NO MODEL, SO NOTHING TO CHECK. Every sentence below is a norm Policy.hs derived, in its policy's own
>#  wording, and the assistant is exactly as correct without a language model as with one — only less warm.
>#  `.after` is empty for a question about now, and ", once you fly," for one asked after the customer's plan.
> if .uncovered:
    No written policy decides this request for booking {{ .reference }}, so I can't promise anything. An agent will review it and contact you.
> else:
    > for norm in .forbidden:
        For booking {{ .reference }}{{ .after }} I can't offer {{ norm.what }}. {{ norm.text }}
    > for norm in .obliged:
        For booking {{ .reference }}{{ .after }} you can have {{ norm.what }}. {{ norm.text }}
    > for lapse in .lapses:
        Until {{ lapse.event }}, you can have {{ lapse.what }}. {{ lapse.text }}
    > if .never:
        So {{ .doing }} first and then getting {{ .asked }} is not possible.
